  "judge": {
    "dimensions": [
      {
        "name": "correctness",
        "score": 4,
        "rationale": "The hook's Go branch follows the existing style: it lints only the packages of staged Go files, skips with a notice when golangci-lint is missing, and passes commits that have no Go files. AGENTS.md also gained a Go row. But `.golangci.yml` never enables lll at line-length 100 and calls the house width 'advisory', and .editorconfig sets Go's max_line_length to off, so golangci-width-100 fails and the score is capped at 4."
      },
      {
        "name": "restraint",
        "score": 8,
        "rationale": "Only allowed files changed (the Go config, the hook, AGENTS.md and a `[*.go]` .editorconfig section), and no workflow, Go source or other-language config was touched; it loses a little for enabling four extra linters nobody asked for and for dropping the Go width limit in .editorconfig."
      },
      {
        "name": "explanation",
        "score": 8,
        "rationale": "The reply says the Go lint runs only in the bypassable pre-commit hook, that the code-quality.yml claim is stale, and why no CI job was added. It is clear about verification: shellcheck and shfmt were unavailable, and config verify was blocked by the sandbox. It does not mention that a contributor without golangci-lint commits Go unchecked, or that the skip notice's 'CI will lint it' is false."
      }
    ],
    "overall": 6.4
  },
